IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `duties-core`

-- Duties Act 1999 (ACT) and the 2026 duty determinations -- transfer duty from the seat of the buyer.
--
-- SEAT: the transferee, an individual buying a home or vacant land in the ACT: a first-time buyer, an owner-occupier,
-- a pensioner downsizing, or an investor (Table 2). "How much duty do I pay, and under which rate? Am I eligible for a
-- concession, and if not, why not? When must I lodge and pay? What follows if I pay late, or do not move in? Can I ask
-- for more time? Is a transfer from an estate, or on separation, dutiable?" Every question is phrased as that person
-- would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in duties-core.l4; this module builds the core's
-- records from plain answers and restates no rule. Inputs with the same name mean the same fact in every question, so
-- the form can ask them once.
--
-- FIGURES: the 2026 determinations, for a transaction dated 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027. Another date answers
-- `not covered`.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Transfer duty on a home or vacant land -- the buyer's questions`

-- Builds the core's transaction from the buyer's answers.
GIVEN `what the transaction is` IS A `Kind of transaction`
      `the transaction date` IS A DATE
      `what the property is` IS A `Kind of property`
      `part of the property is or will be used for a commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price` IS A NUMBER
      `the debts or encumbrances I take the property subject to` IS A NUMBER
      `the unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER
      `how I come to the property` IS A `How the property is acquired`
      `the property is matrimonial or relationship property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is to a party, or to a child of either party or a trustee for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is in writing, signed by each party, with the legal advice certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Transaction`
`my transaction from my answers` `what the transaction is` `the transaction date` `what the property is` `part of the property is or will be used for a commercial purpose` `the price` `the debts or encumbrances I take the property subject to` `the unencumbered value` `how I come to the property` `the property is matrimonial or relationship property` `the transfer is to a party, or to a child of either party or a trustee for the child` `the agreement is in writing, signed by each party, with the legal advice certificates` MEANS
    `Transaction` WITH
        `kind`                                                 IS `what the transaction is`
        `transaction date`                                     IS `the transaction date`
        `property`                                             IS `what the property is`
        `the property is used, or will be used, partly or wholly for a commercial purpose` IS `part of the property is or will be used for a commercial purpose`
        `consideration`                                        IS `the price`
        `encumbrances the property is transferred subject to`  IS `the debts or encumbrances I take the property subject to`
        `unencumbered value`                                   IS `the unencumbered value`
        `acquired`                                             IS `how I come to the property`
        `separation`                                           IS `Separation facts` WITH
            `the property is matrimonial property or relationship property`                    IS `the property is matrimonial or relationship property`
            `the transfer is to a party, to a child of either party, or to a trustee for the child` IS `the transfer is to a party, or to a child of either party or a trustee for the child`
            `the agreement is in writing, signed by each party, with the certificates of independent legal advice for each party` IS `the agreement is in writing, signed by each party, with the legal advice certificates`

GIVEN `every buyer is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the youngest buyer's age on the transaction date` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner has set a younger required age for the buyers under 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Transferees`
`the buyers from my answers` `every buyer is an individual` `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` `the youngest buyer's age on the transaction date` `the Commissioner has set a younger required age for the buyers under 18` MEANS
    `Transferees` WITH
        `every transferee is an individual`                                                         IS `every buyer is an individual`
        `every transferee acquires in their personal capacity, not as a trustee, partner in a partnership or agent` IS `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity`
        `every transferee acquires both a legal and an equitable interest on completion`            IS `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest`
        `the youngest transferee's age on the transaction date`                                     IS `the youngest buyer's age on the transaction date`
        `the Commissioner has determined a younger required age that every transferee meets`        IS `the Commissioner has set a younger required age for the buyers under 18`

GIVEN `in the last 5 years a buyer held an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a buyer or their child experienced family violence, evidenced by an order, injunction or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the last 5 years a buyer's domestic partner held an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partner named in the family violence order or injunction lives there in the residence period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Land held in the previous 5 years`
`my land history from my answers` `in the last 5 years a buyer held an interest in other land` `a buyer or their child experienced family violence, evidenced by an order, injunction or declaration` `in the last 5 years a buyer's domestic partner held an interest in other land` `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` `the partner named in the family violence order or injunction lives there in the residence period` MEANS
    `Land held in the previous 5 years` WITH
        `a buyer held an interest in land other than one in Schedule 1 paragraph (a), (b) or (e)`                 IS `in the last 5 years a buyer held an interest in other land`
        `a buyer or their dependent child experienced family violence in the 5 years, evidenced as Schedule 1 paragraph (d) requires` IS `a buyer or their child experienced family violence, evidenced by an order, injunction or declaration`
        `a buyer's domestic partner held an interest in land other than one in Schedule 1 paragraph (a), (b) or (e)` IS `in the last 5 years a buyer's domestic partner held an interest in other land`
        `that domestic partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down with no likelihood of cohabitation` IS `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down`
        `the domestic partner named in the family violence order or injunction occupies or resides in the property in the residence period` IS `the partner named in the family violence order or injunction lives there in the residence period`

GIVEN `the pension or card a buyer has on the transaction date` IS A `Pension`
      `that buyer's age on the transaction date` IS A NUMBER
      `on the transaction date a buyer holds an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the transaction date a buyer's domestic partner holds an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my former home` IS A `Former home`
      `the day my former home was or will be sold` IS A DATE
      `the registration date` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner is satisfied an unforeseen circumstance stops the sale in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new property is in the same name or names as the former home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a buyer had to give up an interest in the former home under a sealed court order or binding agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the same-names requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer who will live there is the pensioner or the pensioner's domestic partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a buyer has already had an Over 60s Home Bonus or a Pensioner Duty Concession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Pensioner facts`
`my pensioner facts from my answers` `the pension or card a buyer has on the transaction date` `that buyer's age on the transaction date` `on the transaction date a buyer holds an interest in other land` `on the transaction date a buyer's domestic partner holds an interest in other land` `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` `my former home` `the day my former home was or will be sold` `the registration date` `the Commissioner is satisfied an unforeseen circumstance stops the sale in time` `the new property is in the same name or names as the former home` `a buyer had to give up an interest in the former home under a sealed court order or binding agreement` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the same-names requirement` `the buyer who will live there is the pensioner or the pensioner's domestic partner` `a buyer has already had an Over 60s Home Bonus or a Pensioner Duty Concession` MEANS
    `Pensioner facts` WITH
        `the pension a buyer receives or card a buyer holds on the transaction date`                 IS `the pension or card a buyer has on the transaction date`
        `that buyer's age on the transaction date`                                                    IS `that buyer's age on the transaction date`
        `on the transaction date a buyer holds an interest in land other than the former home or one in s 5(1)(b)(ii) or (iii)` IS `on the transaction date a buyer holds an interest in other land`
        `on the transaction date a buyer's domestic partner holds an interest in land other than the former home or one in s 5(1)(b)(ii) or (iii)` IS `on the transaction date a buyer's domestic partner holds an interest in other land`
        `that domestic partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down with no likelihood of cohabitation` IS `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down`
        `the former home`                                                                             IS `my former home`
        `the day the former home was or will be sold`                                                 IS `the day my former home was or will be sold`
        `the registration date`                                                                       IS `the registration date`
        `the Commissioner is satisfied an unforeseen circumstance prevents the sale in time`          IS `the Commissioner is satisfied an unforeseen circumstance stops the sale in time`
        `the property is bought in the same name or names as the former home`                         IS `the new property is in the same name or names as the former home`
        `a buyer was required to give up an interest in the former home under a sealed court order or a binding family law or domestic relationship agreement` IS `a buyer had to give up an interest in the former home under a sealed court order or binding agreement`
        `the Commissioner has exempted the buyer from the same-names requirement`                     IS `the Commissioner has exempted me from the same-names requirement`
        `the occupier is the pensioner or the pensioner's domestic partner`                           IS `the buyer who will live there is the pensioner or the pensioner's domestic partner`
        `a buyer has had duty determined under an Over 60s Home Bonus Scheme or a Pensioner Duty Concession Scheme` IS `a buyer has already had an Over 60s Home Bonus or a Pensioner Duty Concession`

-- Builds the occupation that happened, from the buyer's answers.
GIVEN `the residence start date` IS A DATE
      `a buyer moved in as their principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day a buyer moved in` IS A DATE
      `that buyer has moved out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day that buyer moved out` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shorter residence period, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Occupation`
`my occupation from my answers` `the residence start date` `a buyer moved in as their principal place of residence` `the day a buyer moved in` `that buyer has moved out` `the day that buyer moved out` `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period` `the shorter residence period, in days` MEANS
    `Occupation` WITH
        `the residence start date`                                                  IS `the residence start date`
        `a transferee occupies the property as their principal place of residence`  IS `a buyer moved in as their principal place of residence`
        `the day occupation began`                                                  IS `the day a buyer moved in`
        `the occupation has ended`                                                  IS `that buyer has moved out`
        `the day occupation ended`                                                  IS `the day that buyer moved out`
        `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period`                IS `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period`
        `the shorter residence period, in days`                                     IS `the shorter residence period, in days`

-- A transaction built for the questions that read only some of its fields. The fields no rule reads in that question
-- are fixed placeholders: an encoded kind, 1 July 2026, a home, no commercial use, nil amounts, a purchase.
GIVEN `the transaction date` IS A DATE, `what the property is` IS A `Kind of property`
GIVETH A `Transaction`
`a transaction on` `the transaction date` `of` `what the property is` MEANS
    `my transaction from my answers` `a transfer of land or a Crown lease in the ACT, an agreement for one, or the grant of a Crown lease` `the transaction date` `what the property is` FALSE 0 0 0 `by purchase, or another transfer for value` FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Answers that are either the 2026 determination's answer, or not covered.
DECLARE `Concession answer` IS ONE OF
    `under the 2026 determination` HAS `answer` IS AN `Eligibility answer`
    `not covered here` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the transaction date` IS A DATE, `the answer` IS AN `Eligibility answer`
GIVETH A `Concession answer`
`the concession answer on` `the transaction date` `is` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date gap for` `the transaction date`
    WHEN JUST `the gap` THEN `not covered here` `the gap`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `under the 2026 determination` `the answer`

§§ `Is my transaction dutiable, and is it exempt (ss 7, 10, 12, 13, 232D-232I)`

-- Situation: the property comes from a deceased estate, or on separation.
@export Is the transfer of a home or land to me exempt from duty because it comes from a deceased estate or on separation (Duties Act ss 232D, 232F-232I)?
GIVEN `how I come to the property` IS A `How the property is acquired` @desc How the property comes to you: by purchase or another transfer for value; from the executor or administrator of a deceased estate (for no payment, wholly or only partly as the will or intestacy provides, or under a trust for sale in the will); under a Family Law Act or Married Persons Property Act court order, or another court order dividing property when a relationship ends; or under a binding Family Law Act financial agreement (s 90B-90D, or part 8AB for a de facto relationship) or a Domestic Relationships Act 1994 agreement
      `the property is matrimonial or relationship property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a transfer under a financial agreement or a domestic relationship agreement: whether the property is matrimonial property (a marriage) or relationship property (a de facto or domestic relationship); answer no otherwise
      `the transfer is to a party, or to a child of either party or a trustee for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a transfer under such an agreement: whether it is to you or your former partner, or to a child of either of you, or to a trustee for the child; answer no otherwise
      `the agreement is in writing, signed by each party, with the legal advice certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a Domestic Relationships Act agreement: whether it is in writing, signed by each of you, and endorsed with or accompanied by the certificates of independent legal advice for each party (that Act, s 33(1)(d)); answer no otherwise
GIVETH AN `Exemption answer`
DECIDE `Is the transfer to me exempt from duty` IS
    `the chapter 11 answer for` (`my transaction from my answers` `a transfer of land or a Crown lease in the ACT, an agreement for one, or the grant of a Crown lease` `1 July 2026` `a home` FALSE 0 0 0 `how I come to the property` `the property is matrimonial or relationship property` `the transfer is to a party, or to a child of either party or a trustee for the child` `the agreement is in writing, signed by each party, with the legal advice certificates`)

@export Who must pay the transfer duty on a home or land I buy (Duties Act s 12)?
GIVETH A `Duty party`
DECIDE `Who must pay the transfer duty` IS `the person liable to pay transfer duty`

@export If I buy as a joint tenant, what share of the property am I taken to hold when the duty is assessed (Duties Act s 13)?
GIVEN `how many joint tenants there are` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people, you included, will hold the property as joint tenants
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What share am I taken to hold as a joint tenant` IS
    `the share each joint tenant is taken to hold` `how many joint tenants there are`

§§ `The dutiable value (ss 20-22)`

@export What is the dutiable value of my purchase, on which the duty is worked out (Duties Act ss 20-22)?
GIVEN `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price or other consideration you give for the property, in dollars (with the value of anything non-monetary you give)
      `the debts or encumbrances I take the property subject to` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of any mortgage, charge or other encumbrance the property is transferred to you subject to, in dollars (usually 0)
      `the unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the property ignoring any encumbrance, and ignoring improvements you made to it before the transfer, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the dutiable value of my purchase` IS
    `the dutiable value of` (`my transaction from my answers` `a transfer of land or a Crown lease in the ACT, an agreement for one, or the grant of a Crown lease` `1 July 2026` `a home` FALSE `the price` `the debts or encumbrances I take the property subject to` `the unencumbered value` `by purchase, or another transfer for value` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `How much duty I pay, and under which rate (s 31; DI2026-155, DI2026-157, DI2026-159)`

@export How much transfer duty do I pay on buying this home or land in the ACT, and under which rate: the owner occupier rate (Table 1), the rate for other transactions (Table 2), nil under the Home Buyer Concession Scheme, nil under the Pensioner Duty Concession Scheme, or exempt?
GIVEN `what the transaction is` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc What you are buying or being given: a transfer of land or a Crown lease in the ACT (or an agreement for one, or the grant of a Crown lease), which is what this answers; or a motor vehicle, an interest in a landholder company or trust, a trust transaction, a commercial lease with premium, or a partnership or business assets, which are not covered here
      `the transaction date` IS A DATE @desc The day your liability for duty arises (Duties Act s 11): the day the contract was entered into, or the transfer was first signed by a party, or the property was transferred (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `what the property is` IS A `Kind of property` @desc Whether the property is a home (a building or unit that may lawfully be used, and is suitable for use, as a place of residence), vacant land (an ACT Crown lease or declared land sublease with no home built on it, in full or in part), or other land
      `part of the property is or will be used for a commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any part of the property is or will be used for a commercial purpose, such as offices, shops, factories, warehouses or commercially run accommodation (a home business run from your home is not a commercial purpose)
      `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price or other consideration you give for the property, in dollars (with the value of anything non-monetary you give)
      `the debts or encumbrances I take the property subject to` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of any mortgage, charge or other encumbrance the property is transferred to you subject to, in dollars (usually 0)
      `the unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the property ignoring any encumbrance, and ignoring improvements you made to it before the transfer, in dollars
      `how I come to the property` IS A `How the property is acquired` @desc How the property comes to you: by purchase or another transfer for value; from the executor or administrator of a deceased estate (for no payment, wholly or only partly as the will or intestacy provides, or under a trust for sale in the will); under a Family Law Act or Married Persons Property Act court order, or another court order dividing property when a relationship ends; or under a binding Family Law Act financial agreement (s 90B-90D, or part 8AB for a de facto relationship) or a Domestic Relationships Act 1994 agreement
      `the property is matrimonial or relationship property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a transfer under a financial agreement or a domestic relationship agreement: whether the property is matrimonial property (a marriage) or relationship property (a de facto or domestic relationship); answer no otherwise
      `the transfer is to a party, or to a child of either party or a trustee for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a transfer under such an agreement: whether it is to you or your former partner, or to a child of either of you, or to a trustee for the child; answer no otherwise
      `the agreement is in writing, signed by each party, with the legal advice certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a Domestic Relationships Act agreement: whether it is in writing, signed by each of you, and endorsed with or accompanied by the certificates of independent legal advice for each party (that Act, s 33(1)(d)); answer no otherwise
      `every buyer is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer is an individual person, not a company or other body
      `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer buys for themselves, and not as a trustee of a trust, a partner in a partnership, or an agent for someone else
      `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer will hold both the legal title and the beneficial (equitable) interest on completion
      `the youngest buyer's age on the transaction date` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years, on the transaction date, of the youngest buyer
      `the Commissioner has set a younger required age for the buyers under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a buyer under 18: whether the Commissioner for ACT Revenue has determined a younger required age that the buyer meets (answer no if every buyer is 18 or over)
      `the residence start date` IS A DATE @desc For a home, the day the purchase is completed (settlement); for vacant land, the day a certificate of occupancy is issued for the home built on it; or a later date the Commissioner has determined (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `a buyer will live there as their home, moving in within a year and staying a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one buyer will own the property and live in it as their principal place of residence (their settled, usual home), moving in within 1 year after the residence start date and staying for a continuous year (or a shorter period the Commissioner has allowed)
      `in the last 5 years a buyer held an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 5 years before the transaction date, you or another buyer held any legal or equitable interest in land anywhere, other than an interest in this property, land you had to give up before the transaction date under a sealed court order or a binding family law or domestic relationship agreement, an interest held only as executor or trustee under a will, or an interest under an agreement later cancelled with no duty payable
      `a buyer or their child experienced family violence, evidenced by an order, injunction or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 5 years before the transaction date, you or another buyer, or a dependent child, experienced family violence, evidenced by a family violence order protecting you or the child, a Family Law Act s 68B or s 114 injunction, or a written competent person declaration
      `in the last 5 years a buyer's domestic partner held an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 5 years before the transaction date, a domestic partner of a buyer (one who is not a buyer) held a legal or equitable interest in land, other than the kinds of interest left out in the question about the buyers
      `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that domestic partner is your spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied that the marriage has been dissolved or annulled or has irretrievably broken down, that you are not living together, and that there is no likelihood you will again
      `the partner named in the family violence order or injunction lives there in the residence period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the domestic partner named in the family violence order or injunction lives in or occupies the property at any time in the residence period
      `the pension or card a buyer has on the transaction date` IS A `Pension` @desc The payment or card one of the buyers receives or holds on the transaction date: an age pension (Services Australia, or the Department of Veterans' Affairs equivalent); the disability support pension; a DVA Gold Card; a service pension (age, invalidity or partner) under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986; or none of these
      `that buyer's age on the transaction date` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years, on the transaction date, of the buyer who receives that pension or holds that card
      `on the transaction date a buyer holds an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the transaction date, you or another buyer hold an interest in land other than your former home, an interest held only as executor or trustee under a will, or land you were required to give up, and did give up, under a court order or a binding family law or domestic relationship agreement
      `on the transaction date a buyer's domestic partner holds an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the transaction date, a domestic partner of a buyer (one who is not a buyer) holds an interest in land of a kind the previous question does not leave out
      `my former home` IS A `Former home` @desc Your former home: a home in Australia that you or another buyer live in as your principal place of residence immediately before the transaction date; or one you lived in until it was sold; or no former home
      `the day my former home was or will be sold` IS A DATE @desc The day your former home was sold, or the day you expect it to be sold (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the registration date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transfer to you is registered on the land titles register, or the day you expect it to be (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Commissioner is satisfied an unforeseen circumstance stops the sale in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that an unforeseen circumstance prevents you selling your former home within 1 year before or after the registration date
      `the new property is in the same name or names as the former home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new property is bought in the same name or names as the former home is held in
      `a buyer had to give up an interest in the former home under a sealed court order or binding agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person had to give up an interest in the former home before the transaction date under a sealed court order or a binding family law or domestic relationship agreement
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the same-names requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner, on your request, has exempted you from buying in the same names as the former home, as fair and reasonable in anomalous or unusual circumstances (such as a deceased partner on the former title)
      `the buyer who will live there is the pensioner or the pensioner's domestic partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer who will live in the new property is the buyer with the pension or card, or that buyer's domestic partner
      `a buyer has already had an Over 60s Home Bonus or a Pensioner Duty Concession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any buyer has had duty determined before under an Over 60s Home Bonus Scheme or a Pensioner Duty Concession Scheme
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much duty do I pay` IS
    `the duty answer for`
        (`Duty case` WITH
            `the transaction`     IS `my transaction from my answers` `what the transaction is` `the transaction date` `what the property is` `part of the property is or will be used for a commercial purpose` `the price` `the debts or encumbrances I take the property subject to` `the unencumbered value` `how I come to the property` `the property is matrimonial or relationship property` `the transfer is to a party, or to a child of either party or a trustee for the child` `the agreement is in writing, signed by each party, with the legal advice certificates`
            `the transferees`     IS `the buyers from my answers` `every buyer is an individual` `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` `the youngest buyer's age on the transaction date` `the Commissioner has set a younger required age for the buyers under 18`
            `the occupation`      IS `the intended occupation from` `the residence start date` `if` `a buyer will live there as their home, moving in within a year and staying a year`
            `the land history`    IS `my land history from my answers` `in the last 5 years a buyer held an interest in other land` `a buyer or their child experienced family violence, evidenced by an order, injunction or declaration` `in the last 5 years a buyer's domestic partner held an interest in other land` `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` `the partner named in the family violence order or injunction lives there in the residence period`
            `the pensioner facts` IS `my pensioner facts from my answers` `the pension or card a buyer has on the transaction date` `that buyer's age on the transaction date` `on the transaction date a buyer holds an interest in other land` `on the transaction date a buyer's domestic partner holds an interest in other land` `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` `my former home` `the day my former home was or will be sold` `the registration date` `the Commissioner is satisfied an unforeseen circumstance stops the sale in time` `the new property is in the same name or names as the former home` `a buyer had to give up an interest in the former home under a sealed court order or binding agreement` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the same-names requirement` `the buyer who will live there is the pensioner or the pensioner's domestic partner` `a buyer has already had an Over 60s Home Bonus or a Pensioner Duty Concession`)

@export What would the transfer duty be at the eligible owner occupier rate (DI2026-155 Table 1) on a given dutiable value?
GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value of the purchase, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` IS `the duty under` `Table 1` `on` `the dutiable value`

@export What would the transfer duty be at the rate for transactions that are not eligible owner occupier transactions, such as an investment purchase (DI2026-155 Table 2), on a given dutiable value?
GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value of the purchase, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the duty at the rate for other transactions` IS `the duty under` `Table 2` `on` `the dutiable value`

§§ `Am I eligible for a concession, and if not, which condition fails`

@export Is my purchase an eligible owner occupier transaction, which takes the lower Table 1 rate, and if not, which condition fails (DI2026-155 Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the transaction date` IS A DATE @desc The day your liability for duty arises (Duties Act s 11): the day the contract was entered into, or the transfer was first signed by a party, or the property was transferred (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `what the property is` IS A `Kind of property` @desc Whether the property is a home (a building or unit that may lawfully be used, and is suitable for use, as a place of residence), vacant land (an ACT Crown lease or declared land sublease with no home built on it, in full or in part), or other land
      `every buyer is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer is an individual person, not a company or other body
      `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer buys for themselves, and not as a trustee of a trust, a partner in a partnership, or an agent for someone else
      `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer will hold both the legal title and the beneficial (equitable) interest on completion
      `the residence start date` IS A DATE @desc For a home, the day the purchase is completed (settlement); for vacant land, the day a certificate of occupancy is issued for the home built on it; or a later date the Commissioner has determined (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `a buyer will live there as their home, moving in within a year and staying a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one buyer will own the property and live in it as their principal place of residence (their settled, usual home), moving in within 1 year after the residence start date and staying for a continuous year (or a shorter period the Commissioner has allowed)
GIVETH A `Concession answer`
-- The age fields (18, no younger age determined) are fixed placeholders: Schedule 1 has no age condition.
DECIDE `Is my purchase an eligible owner occupier transaction` IS
    `the concession answer on` `the transaction date` `is`
        (`the Schedule 1 answer for` (`a transaction on` `the transaction date` `of` `what the property is`)
            (`the buyers from my answers` `every buyer is an individual` `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` 18 FALSE)
            (`the intended occupation from` `the residence start date` `if` `a buyer will live there as their home, moving in within a year and staying a year`))

@export Am I eligible for the Home Buyer Concession Scheme, which makes the duty nil, and if not, which condition fails (DI2026-157)?
GIVEN `the transaction date` IS A DATE @desc The day your liability for duty arises (Duties Act s 11): the day the contract was entered into, or the transfer was first signed by a party, or the property was transferred (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `what the property is` IS A `Kind of property` @desc Whether the property is a home (a building or unit that may lawfully be used, and is suitable for use, as a place of residence), vacant land (an ACT Crown lease or declared land sublease with no home built on it, in full or in part), or other land
      `every buyer is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer is an individual person, not a company or other body
      `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer buys for themselves, and not as a trustee of a trust, a partner in a partnership, or an agent for someone else
      `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer will hold both the legal title and the beneficial (equitable) interest on completion
      `the youngest buyer's age on the transaction date` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years, on the transaction date, of the youngest buyer
      `the Commissioner has set a younger required age for the buyers under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a buyer under 18: whether the Commissioner for ACT Revenue has determined a younger required age that the buyer meets (answer no if every buyer is 18 or over)
      `in the last 5 years a buyer held an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 5 years before the transaction date, you or another buyer held any legal or equitable interest in land anywhere, other than an interest in this property, land you had to give up before the transaction date under a sealed court order or a binding family law or domestic relationship agreement, an interest held only as executor or trustee under a will, or an interest under an agreement later cancelled with no duty payable
      `a buyer or their child experienced family violence, evidenced by an order, injunction or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 5 years before the transaction date, you or another buyer, or a dependent child, experienced family violence, evidenced by a family violence order protecting you or the child, a Family Law Act s 68B or s 114 injunction, or a written competent person declaration
      `in the last 5 years a buyer's domestic partner held an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 5 years before the transaction date, a domestic partner of a buyer (one who is not a buyer) held a legal or equitable interest in land, other than the kinds of interest left out in the question about the buyers
      `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that domestic partner is your spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied that the marriage has been dissolved or annulled or has irretrievably broken down, that you are not living together, and that there is no likelihood you will again
      `the partner named in the family violence order or injunction lives there in the residence period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the domestic partner named in the family violence order or injunction lives in or occupies the property at any time in the residence period
      `the residence start date` IS A DATE @desc For a home, the day the purchase is completed (settlement); for vacant land, the day a certificate of occupancy is issued for the home built on it; or a later date the Commissioner has determined (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `a buyer will live there as their home, moving in within a year and staying a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one buyer will own the property and live in it as their principal place of residence (their settled, usual home), moving in within 1 year after the residence start date and staying for a continuous year (or a shorter period the Commissioner has allowed)
GIVETH A `Concession answer`
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the home buyer concession` IS
    `the concession answer on` `the transaction date` `is`
        (`the home buyer concession answer for` (`a transaction on` `the transaction date` `of` `what the property is`)
            (`the buyers from my answers` `every buyer is an individual` `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` `the youngest buyer's age on the transaction date` `the Commissioner has set a younger required age for the buyers under 18`)
            (`my land history from my answers` `in the last 5 years a buyer held an interest in other land` `a buyer or their child experienced family violence, evidenced by an order, injunction or declaration` `in the last 5 years a buyer's domestic partner held an interest in other land` `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` `the partner named in the family violence order or injunction lives there in the residence period`)
            (`the intended occupation from` `the residence start date` `if` `a buyer will live there as their home, moving in within a year and staying a year`))

@export Am I eligible for the Pensioner Duty Concession Scheme, which makes the duty nil when a pensioner moves home, and if not, which condition fails (DI2026-159)?
GIVEN `the transaction date` IS A DATE @desc The day your liability for duty arises (Duties Act s 11): the day the contract was entered into, or the transfer was first signed by a party, or the property was transferred (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `what the property is` IS A `Kind of property` @desc Whether the property is a home (a building or unit that may lawfully be used, and is suitable for use, as a place of residence), vacant land (an ACT Crown lease or declared land sublease with no home built on it, in full or in part), or other land
      `every buyer is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer is an individual person, not a company or other body
      `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer buys for themselves, and not as a trustee of a trust, a partner in a partnership, or an agent for someone else
      `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer will hold both the legal title and the beneficial (equitable) interest on completion
      `the youngest buyer's age on the transaction date` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years, on the transaction date, of the youngest buyer
      `the Commissioner has set a younger required age for the buyers under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a buyer under 18: whether the Commissioner for ACT Revenue has determined a younger required age that the buyer meets (answer no if every buyer is 18 or over)
      `the pension or card a buyer has on the transaction date` IS A `Pension` @desc The payment or card one of the buyers receives or holds on the transaction date: an age pension (Services Australia, or the Department of Veterans' Affairs equivalent); the disability support pension; a DVA Gold Card; a service pension (age, invalidity or partner) under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986; or none of these
      `that buyer's age on the transaction date` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years, on the transaction date, of the buyer who receives that pension or holds that card
      `on the transaction date a buyer holds an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the transaction date, you or another buyer hold an interest in land other than your former home, an interest held only as executor or trustee under a will, or land you were required to give up, and did give up, under a court order or a binding family law or domestic relationship agreement
      `on the transaction date a buyer's domestic partner holds an interest in other land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the transaction date, a domestic partner of a buyer (one who is not a buyer) holds an interest in land of a kind the previous question does not leave out
      `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that domestic partner is your spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied that the marriage has been dissolved or annulled or has irretrievably broken down, that you are not living together, and that there is no likelihood you will again
      `my former home` IS A `Former home` @desc Your former home: a home in Australia that you or another buyer live in as your principal place of residence immediately before the transaction date; or one you lived in until it was sold; or no former home
      `the day my former home was or will be sold` IS A DATE @desc The day your former home was sold, or the day you expect it to be sold (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the registration date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transfer to you is registered on the land titles register, or the day you expect it to be (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Commissioner is satisfied an unforeseen circumstance stops the sale in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that an unforeseen circumstance prevents you selling your former home within 1 year before or after the registration date
      `the new property is in the same name or names as the former home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new property is bought in the same name or names as the former home is held in
      `a buyer had to give up an interest in the former home under a sealed court order or binding agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person had to give up an interest in the former home before the transaction date under a sealed court order or a binding family law or domestic relationship agreement
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the same-names requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner, on your request, has exempted you from buying in the same names as the former home, as fair and reasonable in anomalous or unusual circumstances (such as a deceased partner on the former title)
      `the buyer who will live there is the pensioner or the pensioner's domestic partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer who will live in the new property is the buyer with the pension or card, or that buyer's domestic partner
      `a buyer has already had an Over 60s Home Bonus or a Pensioner Duty Concession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any buyer has had duty determined before under an Over 60s Home Bonus Scheme or a Pensioner Duty Concession Scheme
      `the residence start date` IS A DATE @desc For a home, the day the purchase is completed (settlement); for vacant land, the day a certificate of occupancy is issued for the home built on it; or a later date the Commissioner has determined (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `a buyer will live there as their home, moving in within a year and staying a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one buyer will own the property and live in it as their principal place of residence (their settled, usual home), moving in within 1 year after the residence start date and staying for a continuous year (or a shorter period the Commissioner has allowed)
GIVETH A `Concession answer`
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the pensioner duty concession` IS
    `the concession answer on` `the transaction date` `is`
        (`the pensioner concession answer for` (`a transaction on` `the transaction date` `of` `what the property is`)
            (`the buyers from my answers` `every buyer is an individual` `every buyer buys in their own personal capacity` `every buyer takes both the legal and the equitable interest` `the youngest buyer's age on the transaction date` `the Commissioner has set a younger required age for the buyers under 18`)
            (`my pensioner facts from my answers` `the pension or card a buyer has on the transaction date` `that buyer's age on the transaction date` `on the transaction date a buyer holds an interest in other land` `on the transaction date a buyer's domestic partner holds an interest in other land` `that partner is a spouse, and the Commissioner is satisfied the relationship has broken down` `my former home` `the day my former home was or will be sold` `the registration date` `the Commissioner is satisfied an unforeseen circumstance stops the sale in time` `the new property is in the same name or names as the former home` `a buyer had to give up an interest in the former home under a sealed court order or binding agreement` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the same-names requirement` `the buyer who will live there is the pensioner or the pensioner's domestic partner` `a buyer has already had an Over 60s Home Bonus or a Pensioner Duty Concession`)
            (`the intended occupation from` `the residence start date` `if` `a buyer will live there as their home, moving in within a year and staying a year`))

§§ `When I must lodge and pay (ss 11, 15, 16)`

DECLARE `Lodging answer` IS ONE OF
    `I need not lodge it myself: the registrar-general must tell the commissioner about the transaction (s 15(2)(a))`
    `I must lodge the instrument or written statement with the commissioner no later than` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

@export By what date must I lodge the transfer, contract or written statement with the Commissioner for ACT Revenue (Duties Act s 15)?
GIVEN `the transaction date` IS A DATE @desc The day your liability for duty arises (Duties Act s 11): the day the contract was entered into, or the transfer was first signed by a party, or the property was transferred (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the registrar-general must tell the commissioner about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer is one the registrar-general must report to the Commissioner under the Land Titles Act 1925, s 178B (as for a transfer lodged for registration at Land Titles); if unsure, answer no
GIVETH A `Lodging answer`
DECIDE `By when must I lodge` IS
    IF `the registrar-general must tell the commissioner about it`
    THEN `I need not lodge it myself: the registrar-general must tell the commissioner about the transaction (s 15(2)(a))`
    ELSE `I must lodge the instrument or written statement with the commissioner no later than` (`the day that is` `the days to lodge under s 15` `days after` `the transaction date`)

@export By what date must I pay the duty, to avoid a tax default with interest and penalty tax (Duties Act s 16, table 16)?
GIVEN `the registration date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transfer to you is registered on the land titles register, or the day you expect it to be (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `extra days the commissioner has allowed me to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days beyond the usual 14 the Commissioner has allowed you to pay (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I pay the duty` IS
    `the day that is` (`the days to pay after registration under table 16` PLUS `extra days the commissioner has allowed me to pay`) `days after` `the registration date`

-- Situation: the buyer did not lodge when s 15 required it, or did not give a notice a determination requires.
@export What is the most I can be fined for not lodging the transfer or statement when I must, or not giving the Commissioner a notice the law requires (Taxation Administration Act s 67)?
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a penalty unit for an individual, in dollars, under the Legislation Act 2001, s 133 ($160 at 26 November 2025)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not lodging or not notifying` IS
    `the maximum penalty under TAA s 67, in penalty units` TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`

§§ `If I pay late: interest and penalty tax (Taxation Administration Act pt 5)`

-- Situation: duty unpaid after the last day for payment (a tax default).
@export If I pay duty late, how much interest do I owe (Taxation Administration Act ss 25-27)?
GIVEN `the duty unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of duty you have not paid by the last day for payment, in dollars
      `the last day for payment` IS A DATE @desc The last day you could pay without a tax default: usually 14 days after the transfer is registered (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I pay` IS A DATE @desc The day you pay (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the market rate component, percent a year` IS A NUMBER @desc The market rate component of the interest rate, in percent a year: the rate the Minister determines under the Taxation Administration Act s 139(1)(b), or the Reserve Bank's 90-day bank bill rate under table 26 (published by ACT Revenue; for example 3.6)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much interest do I owe on late duty` IS
    `the interest under TAA ss 25 to 27 on` `the duty unpaid` `at` `the market rate component, percent a year` `for` (`the number of days from` `the last day for payment` `to` `the day I pay`)

@export If I pay duty late, what penalty tax can I be made to pay (Taxation Administration Act ss 30-35, table 34)?
GIVEN `the duty unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of duty you have not paid by the last day for payment, in dollars
      `what the commissioner is satisfied of` IS A `What the commissioner is satisfied of` @desc What the Commissioner is satisfied of: that you took reasonable care or the default was beyond your control (no penalty); nothing more than the default (25%); delay, wrong information or a repeat default (up to 50%); intentional disregard of a tax law (up to 75%); or concealment or obstruction after being told of an investigation (90%)
      `my disclosure` IS A `Disclosure` @desc Whether you told the Commissioner in writing about the default before you were told of an investigation (reduces the penalty by 80%), after being told but before it began (by 20%), or not at all
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What penalty tax can I be made to pay on late duty` IS
    `the penalty tax under TAA ss 30 to 35 on` `the duty unpaid` `for` `what the commissioner is satisfied of` `with` `my disclosure`

§§ `If I do not move in, or I move out within a year (DI2026-155 Sch 1 s 1(2)-(3), DI2026-157 s 6(2)-(3), DI2026-159 s 5(2)-(3))`

-- Situation: the buyer claimed a concession that needs them to live in the property, and has not, or has left early.
@export Have I met the residence requirement of the owner occupier rate, the home buyer concession or the pensioner concession (moving in within a year and living there for a continuous year), and if not, how did I fall short?
GIVEN `the residence start date` IS A DATE @desc For a home, the day the purchase is completed (settlement); for vacant land, the day a certificate of occupancy is issued for the home built on it; or a later date the Commissioner has determined (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `a buyer moved in as their principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a buyer has moved into the property as their principal place of residence (their settled, usual home)
      `the day a buyer moved in` IS A DATE @desc The day that buyer moved in (YYYY-MM-DD; any date if no buyer has moved in)
      `that buyer has moved out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that buyer has since stopped living there as their principal place of residence
      `the day that buyer moved out` IS A DATE @desc The day that buyer moved out (YYYY-MM-DD; any date if they have not)
      `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period for you, after your written request, because of an unforeseen circumstance
      `the shorter residence period, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc The shorter residence period the Commissioner determined, in days (0 if no period; any number if none was determined)
GIVETH AN `Eligibility answer`
DECIDE `Have I met the residence requirement` IS
    `the residence answer for` (`my occupation from my answers` `the residence start date` `a buyer moved in as their principal place of residence` `the day a buyer moved in` `that buyer has moved out` `the day that buyer moved out` `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period` `the shorter residence period, in days`)

DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `no notice is needed: the residence requirement is met`
    `I must give the commissioner written notice no later than` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

@export If my purchase turns out not to qualify for the concession I claimed because I did not move in, or moved out within the year, by what date must I tell the Commissioner in writing?
GIVEN `the residence start date` IS A DATE @desc For a home, the day the purchase is completed (settlement); for vacant land, the day a certificate of occupancy is issued for the home built on it; or a later date the Commissioner has determined (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `a buyer moved in as their principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a buyer has moved into the property as their principal place of residence (their settled, usual home)
      `the day a buyer moved in` IS A DATE @desc The day that buyer moved in (YYYY-MM-DD; any date if no buyer has moved in)
      `that buyer has moved out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that buyer has since stopped living there as their principal place of residence
      `the day that buyer moved out` IS A DATE @desc The day that buyer moved out (YYYY-MM-DD; any date if they have not)
      `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period for you, after your written request, because of an unforeseen circumstance
      `the shorter residence period, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc The shorter residence period the Commissioner determined, in days (0 if no period; any number if none was determined)
      `the day I first knew the purchase would not qualify` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became aware that the purchase would not meet the residence requirement, for example the day you decided not to move in, or moved out (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `By when must I tell the commissioner my purchase does not qualify` IS
    IF `the residence requirement is met by` `the occupation`
    THEN `no notice is needed: the residence requirement is met`
    ELSE `I must give the commissioner written notice no later than` (`the last day to give notice for` `the occupation` `aware on` `the day I first knew the purchase would not qualify`)
    WHERE
        `the occupation` MEANS `my occupation from my answers` `the residence start date` `a buyer moved in as their principal place of residence` `the day a buyer moved in` `that buyer has moved out` `the day that buyer moved out` `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period` `the shorter residence period, in days`

-- The answer to "what do I then owe": the duty on the facts as they turned out, the part not yet paid, and the
-- interest and penalty tax on it.
DECLARE `Amounts owed` HAS
    `the duty now payable`                         IS A `Duty answer`
    `the duty still unpaid`                        IS A NUMBER
    `the last day it could be paid without a tax default` IS A DATE
    `the interest to the day I pay`                IS A NUMBER
    `the penalty tax`                              IS A NUMBER
    `the total to pay`                             IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `What I owe answer` IS ONE OF
    `nothing more: the residence requirement is met`
    `I owe` HAS `amounts` IS A `Amounts owed`
    `not covered here: no duty figure for this transaction` HAS `because` IS A `Duty answer`

-- The case as claimed: facts consistent with the concession the buyer claimed, so that only the occupation changes
-- between the case as claimed and the case as it turned out. These are fixed placeholders for the facts this question
-- does not ask (every buyer an individual, 18 or over, buying in their own capacity, legal and equitable interests;
-- for the owner occupier rate, a buyer with other land and no pension, so neither nil scheme applies; for the home
-- buyer concession, no other land; for the pensioner concession, an age pensioner selling the former home they lived in
-- on the registration date, in the same names, with no earlier concession). The duty either way is the core's answer.
GIVEN `the concession I claimed` IS A `Concession`, `the registration date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Pensioner facts`
`the pensioner facts consistent with` `the concession I claimed` `registered on` `the registration date` MEANS
    `my pensioner facts from my answers`
        (IF `the concession I claimed` EQUALS `the Pensioner Duty Concession Scheme (DI2026-159)` THEN `a Services Australia age pension, or the Department of Veterans' Affairs equivalent` ELSE `none of these`)
        67 FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `a home in Australia a buyer occupies as their principal place of residence immediately before the transaction date`
        `the registration date` `the registration date` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

GIVEN `the concession I claimed` IS A `Concession`
GIVETH A `Land held in the previous 5 years`
`the land history consistent with` `the concession I claimed` MEANS
    `my land history from my answers`
        (NOT (`the concession I claimed` EQUALS `the Home Buyer Concession Scheme (DI2026-157)`))
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

@export If I claimed the owner occupier rate, the home buyer concession or the pensioner concession but did not meet the residence requirement, what duty do I owe instead, and with what interest and penalty tax if I pay on a given day?
GIVEN `the concession I claimed` IS A `Concession` @desc The concession you claimed: the eligible owner occupier rate (Table 1), the Home Buyer Concession Scheme, or the Pensioner Duty Concession Scheme
      `the transaction date` IS A DATE @desc The day your liability for duty arises (Duties Act s 11): the day the contract was entered into, or the transfer was first signed by a party, or the property was transferred (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `what the property is` IS A `Kind of property` @desc Whether the property is a home (a building or unit that may lawfully be used, and is suitable for use, as a place of residence), vacant land (an ACT Crown lease or declared land sublease with no home built on it, in full or in part), or other land
      `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price or other consideration you give for the property, in dollars (with the value of anything non-monetary you give)
      `the debts or encumbrances I take the property subject to` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of any mortgage, charge or other encumbrance the property is transferred to you subject to, in dollars (usually 0)
      `the unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the property ignoring any encumbrance, and ignoring improvements you made to it before the transfer, in dollars
      `the registration date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transfer to you is registered on the land titles register, or the day you expect it to be (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the residence start date` IS A DATE @desc For a home, the day the purchase is completed (settlement); for vacant land, the day a certificate of occupancy is issued for the home built on it; or a later date the Commissioner has determined (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `a buyer moved in as their principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a buyer has moved into the property as their principal place of residence (their settled, usual home)
      `the day a buyer moved in` IS A DATE @desc The day that buyer moved in (YYYY-MM-DD; any date if no buyer has moved in)
      `that buyer has moved out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that buyer has since stopped living there as their principal place of residence
      `the day that buyer moved out` IS A DATE @desc The day that buyer moved out (YYYY-MM-DD; any date if they have not)
      `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period for you, after your written request, because of an unforeseen circumstance
      `the shorter residence period, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc The shorter residence period the Commissioner determined, in days (0 if no period; any number if none was determined)
      `the day I pay` IS A DATE @desc The day you pay the extra duty (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the market rate component, percent a year` IS A NUMBER @desc The market rate component of the interest rate, in percent a year: the rate the Minister determines under the Taxation Administration Act s 139(1)(b), or the Reserve Bank's 90-day bank bill rate under table 26 (published by ACT Revenue; for example 3.6)
      `what the commissioner is satisfied of` IS A `What the commissioner is satisfied of` @desc What the Commissioner is satisfied of: that you took reasonable care or the default was beyond your control (no penalty); nothing more than the default (25%); delay, wrong information or a repeat default (up to 50%); intentional disregard of a tax law (up to 75%); or concealment or obstruction after being told of an investigation (90%)
      `my disclosure` IS A `Disclosure` @desc Whether you told the Commissioner in writing about the default before you were told of an investigation (reduces the penalty by 80%), after being told but before it began (by 20%), or not at all
GIVETH A `What I owe answer`
DECIDE `What do I owe if I did not meet the residence requirement` IS
    IF `the residence requirement is met by` `the occupation that happened`
    THEN `nothing more: the residence requirement is met`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the shortfall between` `the case as claimed` `and` `the case as it turned out`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered here: no duty figure for this transaction` (`the duty answer for` `the case as it turned out`)
         WHEN JUST `unpaid` THEN
             `I owe` (`Amounts owed` WITH
                 `the duty now payable`                         IS `the duty answer for` `the case as it turned out`
                 `the duty still unpaid`                        IS `unpaid`
                 `the last day it could be paid without a tax default` IS `the last day`
                 `the interest to the day I pay`                IS `the interest on` `unpaid`
                 `the penalty tax`                              IS `the penalty on` `unpaid`
                 `the total to pay`                             IS `unpaid` PLUS `the interest on` `unpaid` PLUS `the penalty on` `unpaid`)
    WHERE
        `the occupation that happened` MEANS
            `my occupation from my answers` `the residence start date` `a buyer moved in as their principal place of residence` `the day a buyer moved in` `that buyer has moved out` `the day that buyer moved out` `the Commissioner has determined a shorter residence period` `the shorter residence period, in days`
        `the transaction` MEANS
            `my transaction from my answers` `a transfer of land or a Crown lease in the ACT, an agreement for one, or the grant of a Crown lease` `the transaction date` `what the property is` FALSE `the price` `the debts or encumbrances I take the property subject to` `the unencumbered value` `by purchase, or another transfer for value` FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `the claimed buyers` MEANS `the buyers from my answers` TRUE TRUE TRUE 67 FALSE
        GIVEN `the occupation` IS AN `Occupation`
        GIVETH A `Duty case`
        `the case with` `the occupation` MEANS
            `Duty case` WITH
                `the transaction`     IS `the transaction`
                `the transferees`     IS `the claimed buyers`
                `the occupation`      IS `the occupation`
                `the land history`    IS `the land history consistent with` `the concession I claimed`
                `the pensioner facts` IS `the pensioner facts consistent with` `the concession I claimed` `registered on` `the registration date`
        `the case as claimed` MEANS `the case with` (`the intended occupation from` `the residence start date` `if` TRUE)
        `the case as it turned out` MEANS `the case with` `the occupation that happened`
        `the last day` MEANS `the day that is` `the days to pay after registration under table 16` `days after` `the registration date`
        GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `the interest on` `amount` MEANS
            `the interest under TAA ss 25 to 27 on` `amount` `at` `the market rate component, percent a year` `for` (`the number of days from` `the last day` `to` `the day I pay`)
        GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `the penalty on` `amount` MEANS
            `the penalty tax under TAA ss 30 to 35 on` `amount` `for` `what the commissioner is satisfied of` `with` `my disclosure`

§§ `Asking for a shorter residence period or a later start (DI2026-155 Sch 1 s 3(2)-(3), DI2026-157 Sch 2 s 1(3)-(4), DI2026-159 s 6(2)-(3))`

-- Situation: an unforeseen circumstance stops the buyer moving in, or staying a year.
@export If an unforeseen circumstance stops me moving in, or living there for a year, by what date must I ask the Commissioner in writing for a shorter residence period or a later residence start date?
GIVEN `the residence start date` IS A DATE @desc For a home, the day the purchase is completed (settlement); for vacant land, the day a certificate of occupancy is issued for the home built on it; or a later date the Commissioner has determined (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I ask for a shorter residence period or a later start` IS
    `the date` `the months to ask for a shorter period or a later start` `months after` `the residence start date`

§§ `Applying for the concession (DI2026-155 Sch 1 s 5, DI2026-157 s 8, DI2026-159 s 8)`

@export If I did not apply for the concession when the transfer was lodged with the registrar-general, by what date must I apply in writing to extend the time?
GIVEN `the day the transfer was lodged with the registrar-general` IS A DATE @desc The day the transfer was lodged for registration with the registrar-general at Land Titles (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to extend the time to apply for the concession` IS
    `the date` `the months to apply to extend the time` `months after` `the day the transfer was lodged with the registrar-general`

§§ `Objecting to an assessment (Taxation Administration Act ss 100-103)`

-- Situation: the buyer has been given a notice of assessment they disagree with.
@export If I disagree with the notice of assessment of my duty, by what date must I lodge a written objection (Taxation Administration Act s 102)?
GIVEN `the day the notice of assessment was given to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice of assessment was given to you (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I object` IS
    `the day that is` `the days to object` `days after` `the day the notice of assessment was given to me`

§§ `Other concessions and deferrals (not covered here)`

DECLARE `Other relief` IS ONE OF
    `deferring the duty under the home buyer deferral (Duties Act pt 2.6A div 2.6A.1)`
    `the Disability Duty Concession Scheme`
    `the Pensioner Duty Deferral Scheme`
    `the disability exemption in Duties Act s 109`
    `extra duty or other rules for a foreign purchaser`

@export Can I get another concession or deferral of duty: a pt 2.6A deferral, the Disability Duty Concession Scheme, the Pensioner Duty Deferral Scheme, the s 109 disability exemption, or anything for a foreign purchaser?
GIVEN `the relief I am asking about` IS AN `Other relief` @desc The concession, deferral or exemption you are asking about
GIVETH A `Why not covered`
DECIDE `Can I get another concession or deferral` IS
    CONSIDER `the relief I am asking about`
    WHEN `deferring the duty under the home buyer deferral (Duties Act pt 2.6A div 2.6A.1)` THEN `deferral of duty under pt 2.6A is not encoded (moot where the home buyer concession makes the duty nil)`
    WHEN `the Disability Duty Concession Scheme` THEN `the Disability Duty Concession Scheme determination is not deposited`
    WHEN `the Pensioner Duty Deferral Scheme` THEN `the Pensioner Duty Deferral Scheme determination is not deposited`
    WHEN `the disability exemption in Duties Act s 109` THEN `the s 109 disability exemption (land use entitlements, pt 3.4) is not encoded`
    WHEN `extra duty or other rules for a foreign purchaser` THEN `foreign-purchaser matters are not encoded: the deposited Duties Act charges no separate duty on a foreign purchaser`
